{"path":"memory/polymorphic_allocator/new_object","title":"std::pmr::polymorphic_allocator<T>::new_object","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::pmr::polymorphic_allocator&lt;T&gt;::</span>new_object","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/polymorphic_allocator/new_object","section":"memory","kind":"page","summary":"Allocates and constructs an object of type U.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> U, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span>... <span class=\"me1\">CtorArgs</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br>U<span class=\"sy2\">*</span> new_object<span class=\"br0\">(</span> CtorArgs<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span>... <span class=\"me1\">ctor_args</span> <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Allocates and constructs an object of type <code>U</code>.\n</p><p>Given <code>alloc</code> is a <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/polymorphic_allocator\"><span class=\"kw711\">std::<span class=\"me2\">pmr</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">polymorphic_allocator</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span></code>:\n</p>\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code>U<span class=\"sy2\">*</span> p <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> alloc.<span class=\"me1\">new_object</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>U<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/forward\"><span class=\"kw1125\">std::<span class=\"me2\">forward</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>CtorArgs<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>ctor_args<span class=\"br0\">)</span>...<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></code></pre>\n<p>is equivalent to \n</p>\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code>U<span class=\"sy2\">*</span> p <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> alloc.<span class=\"me1\">allocate_object</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>U<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"kw1\">try</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    alloc.<span class=\"me1\">construct</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>p, <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/forward\"><span class=\"kw1125\">std::<span class=\"me2\">forward</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>CtorArgs<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>ctor_args<span class=\"br0\">)</span>...<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n<span class=\"kw1\">catch</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>...<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    alloc.<span class=\"me1\">deallocate_object</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>p<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">throw</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> ctor_args\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> the arguments to forward to the constructor of <code>U</code>\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>A pointer to the allocated and constructed object. \n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>This function was introduced for use with the fully-specialized allocator <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/polymorphic_allocator\"><span class=\"kw711\">std::<span class=\"me2\">pmr</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">polymorphic_allocator</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&gt;</span></span></code>, but it may be useful in any specialization as a shortcut to avoid having to rebind from <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/polymorphic_allocator\"><span class=\"kw711\">std::<span class=\"me2\">pmr</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">polymorphic_allocator</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span></code> to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/polymorphic_allocator\"><span class=\"kw711\">std::<span class=\"me2\">pmr</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">polymorphic_allocator</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>U<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span></code>, and having to call <span class=\"t-lc\">allocate</span>, <span class=\"t-lc\">construct</span>, and <span class=\"t-lc\">deallocate</span> individually.\n</p><p>Since <code>U</code> is not deduced, it must be provided as a template argument when calling this function.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\n<p>May throw any exceptions thrown by the call to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">allocate_object</span></code> or the constructor of <code>U</code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/polymorphic_allocator/allocate_bytes\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>allocate_bytes</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  allocate raw aligned memory from the underlying resource <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/polymorphic_allocator/allocate_object\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>allocate_object</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  allocates raw memory suitable for an object or an array <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/polymorphic_allocator/allocate\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>allocate</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  allocate memory <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/allocator_traits/allocate\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>allocate</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-cmark\">[static]</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  allocates uninitialized storage using the allocator <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public static member function of <code>std::allocator_traits&lt;Alloc&gt;</code>)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/memory_resource/allocate\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>allocate</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  allocates memory <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function of <code>std::pmr::memory_resource</code>)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"memory","title":"Memory management library"},{"path":"memory/polymorphic_allocator","title":"std::pmr::polymorphic_allocator"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::pmr::polymorphic_allocator<T>::new_object","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++20. Allocates and constructs an object of type U."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"ctor_args"},{"label":"Return value","note":"A pointer to the allocated and constructed object."},{"label":"Notes","note":"This function was introduced for use with the fully-specialized allocator std::pmr::polymorphic_allocator<>, but it may be useful in any specialization as a…"},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"May throw any exceptions thrown by the call to allocate_object or the constructor of U."},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"allocate_bytes","note":"allocate raw aligned memory from the underlying resource"},{"label":"allocate_object","note":"allocates raw memory suitable for an object or an array"},{"label":"allocate","note":"allocate memory"},{"label":"allocate","note":"allocates uninitialized storage using the allocator"},{"label":"allocate","note":"allocates memory"}]}]},"standards":["C++20"],"wordCount":198,"codeBlockCount":2}
